  "supersededRows": [
    {
      "file": "batch-02-coding",
      "benchmark": "deepswe",
      "supersededBy": "batch-11-deepswe",
      "reason": "Batch 02 transcribed the DeepSWE board by eye: 18 rows of its 'Best view', rounded to whole points (74 where the artifact says 73.6). Batch 11 reads the same page's own artifact and gets all 50 configurations at full precision. These are not two measurements, they are one measurement read twice, so ingesting both would put two rows in one cell and let the rounded one win the primary slot -- a system benchmark keeps the highest score within a source class, and 74 beats 73.6. The rows stay in the archive because they are real evidence of what the page showed on 2026-07-31."
    },
    {
      "file": "batch-02-coding",
      "benchmark": "terminal",
      "benchmarkVersion": "2.1",
      "supersededBy": "batch-13-terminal-bench",
      "reason": "Batch 02 transcribed the Terminal-Bench 2.1 board by eye. Batch 13 reads the Supabase function the page itself calls, which returns the same submissions with the agent, reasoning effort, run date, trial count and pass@k attached. One measurement read twice, so only the scripted reading is ingested. Scoped to version 2.1 deliberately: batch 02 also holds Terminal-Bench 2.0 rows under the same benchmark name, they map to the separate terminal-20 column, and no scripted source replaces them."
    },
    {
      "file": "batch-08-operating",
      "modelRaw": "Inkling",
      "field": "context_k",
      "supersededBy": "batch-15-model-config",
      "reason": "256K is the Tinker Serverless Inference product serving limit (the pricing page lists it per product tier), not the model's architectural context window. The architectural maximum (1,048,576 from HF config.json model_max_length) is carried in batch-15. Both values are real published facts and both stay in the archive unchanged; this entry tells the provenance check to use batch-15 for the context_k field, so the catalog's 1000K is backed rather than disputed. Scoped to modelRaw + field so other models in batch-08 are unaffected."
    },
    {
      "file": "batch-08-operating",
      "modelRaw": "Inkling-Small",
      "field": "context_k",
      "supersededBy": "batch-15-model-config",
      "reason": "Same as Inkling above: 256K is the Serverless Inference serving limit, not the context window. config.json model_max_length is 1,048,576 (batch-15). Both stay in the archive; this entry routes the provenance check to batch-15 for this field."
    },
    {
      "file": "batch-01-reasoning-math",
      "benchmark": "gpqa",
      "benchmarkVersion": "Diamond",
      "supersededBy": "batch-12-epoch",
      "reason": "Batch 01 transcribed the Epoch GPQA Diamond board by eye: 20 rows with the reasoning effort folded into the model string and scores rounded to one decimal. Batch 12 reads Epoch's own hub export and gets the same board at full precision with effort in its own field. One measurement read twice, so only the scripted reading is ingested -- gpt-5.5 (xhigh) 94.0 is batch 12's 94, GPT-5.5 Pro (xhigh) 93.9 is 93.92, GPT-5.5 (low) 90.7 is 90.66, and DeepSeek v4 (max) 89.6 is deepseek-v4-pro's 89.65. Comparing the two batches by model string understates the overlap, because only batch 01 writes the effort into the name; the correspondence is by model plus effort. The rows stay in the archive unchanged."
    }
